---
/**
 * Merges the old /about (facility facts) and /our-story (voice). The /our-story
 * voice is the best writing on the site — "six feet of Minnesota sadness",
 * "Apparently having multiple locations means you're supposed to look
 * professional or something" — and it matches the segment rule that warm and
 * slightly irreverent beats premium and serious (playbook-sim-venue.md §2). It
 * is kept close to verbatim rather than rewritten into brochure prose.
 *
 * ⚠️ RESTORED TO FIRST PERSON 2026-08-04 (FW-4000), from
 * `_ingest/raw/our-story.html`, approved for reuse.
 *
 * We had it in the third person — "CJ had run outdoor golf leagues" — which is
 * the one edit that costs the whole thing. It is CJ's account of the pair of
 * them, and reported speech turns a founder telling you a story into a brochure
 * describing two founders. Four of the best jokes had also quietly gone: the
 * toil-paper aside, "borderline obsessed", the Windows 98 modem noise, and
 * "with enough vision, determination, and updated operating systems". They are
 * back, in their words.
 *
 * Facts are unchanged and still carry their sources: December 2021, the LLC in
 * January 2022, Lakeville open autumn 2022, Stillwater open February 2026
 * (which agrees with `venues/stillwater.json`, and is more precise than the
 * "early 2026" we had). Spelling follows the site's existing British house
 * style, as every other page does; the jokes, the rhythm and the asides are
 * theirs verbatim.
 *
 * This page also has an SEO job: "Lakeville Links" still outranks "The Links"
 * in branded demand and will for a year. The old name has to appear in body
 * copy here so the brand-transition query resolves on this site rather than on a
 * directory (seo-map.md §1.3). Do NOT purge it.
 *
 * #press and #sponsors are redirect targets for the retired /news and
 * /advertisinglogos pages (seo-map.md §4), so the anchors must stay stable.
 *
 * Press is cited as links only. No quote is attributed to any outlet that was
 * not captured verbatim, and none was.
 *
 * ── STUB PASS 2026-08-05 (FW-4013) ─────────────────────────────────────────
 *
 * Three raw `STUB —` blocks rendered here in production, under real section
 * headings. Two of them were tasks of ours and are now `StubNote`s: chase the
 * outlets for pull quotes, chase Google for review permalinks. Neither is a
 * visitor's business.
 *
 * The sponsors one is different, and it is the reason this page is worth reading
 * carefully. Buried in it was a FACT: Bay 3 has no sponsor. Five bays are listed
 * and they run 1, 2, 4, 5, 6 — anybody who counts notices, and hiding the note
 * would have left the site looking as though it could not count rather than as
 * though a bay is unsold. So the missing bay is marked with the gap system and
 * stays visible; the logo files, the websites and the trading names are ours to
 * chase and go in the `StubNote`.
 */
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BookButton from '../components/venue/BookButton.astro';
import GapCell from '../components/venue/GapCell.astro';
import StubNote from '../components/venue/StubNote.astro';
import { getVenues, venuePath } from '../lib/venues';

const venues = await getVenues();
const testimonials = (await getCollection('testimonials')).sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order);

const metadata = {
  metaTitle: 'About The Links — Indoor Golf in Lakeville & Stillwater',
  metaDescription:
    'Two neighbours, one long Minnesota winter, now two clubhouses — Lakeville since 2022, Stillwater since 2026. The story, the press, the sponsors.',
};

/**
 * Coverage. Titles, outlets and dates as published — links, not pull quotes.
 *
 * The two YouTube entries carry the TITLE OF THE VIDEO, confirmed first-hand
 * through YouTube's oEmbed endpoint (which also returns
 * `author_name: "twincitiesgolf"`, so the outlet credit is sound). They used to
 * carry the client's own blog-post headlines instead, which credited
 * TwinCitiesGolf with a headline TwinCitiesGolf did not write — in a section
 * called "In the press". If a link changes, re-resolve the title from oEmbed;
 * do not retype it from the client's blog. See truth-audit.md §U22.
 */
const press = [
  {
    outlet: 'TwinCitiesGolf.com',
    title: 'FIRST LOOK at The Links of Stillwater Indoor Golf Simulators in Stillwater, Minnesota',
    date: '2026',
    href: 'https://www.twincitiesgolf.com/news/the-links-of-stillwater-indoor-golf-simulators-in-stillwater-minnesota',
  },
  {
    outlet: 'TwinCitiesGolf.com',
    title: 'Lakeville Links Indoor Golf Simulator Facility in Lakeville Minnesota',
    date: '25 October 2022',
    href: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3_T1b032Zew',
  },
  {
    outlet: 'TwinCitiesGolf.com',
    title: 'Pre-Opening Sneak Peek Inside Lakeville Links Indoor Golf Simulator',
    date: '19 October 2022',
    href: 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WXRRgKPt4lM',
  },
  {
    outlet: 'Sun ThisWeek',
    title: 'Lakeville Links golf simulator business may open by August',
    date: '25 April 2022',
    href: 'https://www.hometownsource.com/sun_thisweek/community/lakeville/lakeville-links-golf-simulator-business-may-open-by-august/article_f2a604b8-c190-11ec-b825-5f8dcde4e300.html',
  },
];

/** Bay sponsors at Lakeville. Local businesses, on the bays, by name. */
const sponsors = [
  { bay: 'Bay 1', name: 'Align' },
  { bay: 'Bay 2', name: 'Thor' },
  { bay: 'Bay 4', name: 'Von Hanson' },
  { bay: 'Bay 5', name: 'Miller' },
  { bay: 'Bay 6', name: 'Kretsch' },
];
---

<BaseLayout metadata={metadata}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-content px-gutter py-section lg:px-gutter-lg">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold lg:text-5xl">About The Links</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg text-inkMuted">
      Two guys who wanted a better golf simulator to play on during the long Minnesota winters. That is genuinely the
      whole origin story, and the rest of this page is CJ telling it.
    </p>

    {
      /* 1. The story, in the founders' own words and their own voice. First
        person, because it is CJ's account and reported speech flattens it. */
    }
    <div class="mt-section max-w-prose-page">
      <p class="caps-label text-inkMuted">CJ &amp; Cody</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold">Our story</h2>

      <p class="mt-4 text-inkMuted">
        It all started in December 2021. I (CJ) had run outdoor golf leagues for years, and both Cody and I played every
        Wednesday night through the summer. As neighbours and friends, when winter rolled round and golf season
        disappeared into six feet of Minnesota sadness, we kept the Wednesday tradition alive with what we called
        bourbon nights. Because apparently that is what golfers do when there is snow on the ground.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-inkMuted">
        One night, after visiting an indoor golf simulator, we looked at each other and said, "there has to be a better
        option for the Lakeville area." Cody had actually considered opening a simulator place before COVID, but like
        most people during COVID, he had bigger things to worry about — like whether toilet paper had become currency.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-inkMuted">
        The next week I brought it up again. Cody was still casually thinking about it, but as an avid golfer with
        absolutely no ability to let an idea go, I became borderline obsessed. Then we found out a mutual acquaintance
        of Cody's had opened a golf simulator, and suddenly the idea came back to life.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-inkMuted">
        So we started touring golf simulator businesses around the Twin Cities. Every place we visited made us think,
        "this doesn't look THAT hard." Spoiler alert: it was.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-inkMuted">
        After doing our due diligence — and probably not enough sleep — we decided to take the leap. We formed the LLC
        in January 2022 and immediately began looking for space. Then came the challenge of choosing the technology.
        After visiting several venues we landed on GolfZon, because it felt the most immersive and realistic: basically
        the closest thing to real golf without losing balls in the woods or blaming your driver for everything.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-inkMuted">
        Our goal was simple. Create the best golf experience possible, paired with great food, cold drinks, and a place
        people actually wanted to hang out in. <strong>We finally opened in the autumn of 2022.</strong> And honestly, for
        an IT professional and a commodity broker pretending to know how to open an entertainment business, we think we did
        pretty okay.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-3xl font-bold">Then came Stillwater</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-inkMuted">
        Through a mutual connection, an opportunity presented itself. The owner of the Stillwater Bowl had some old golf
        simulators and did not know what to do with them. And when we say old, we mean OLD. The software was literally
        running on Windows 98. We half expected the startup sound to begin with the old modem noises. You know if you
        know.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-inkMuted">
        After more planning, more due diligence, and several conversations that started with "are we really doing this
        again?", we realised it was actually a great opportunity. We saw a chance to bring the Stillwater golf community
        a fun place to play, hang out, and survive the long Minnesota winters without completely losing their golf swing
        — or their sanity. <strong>So in February 2026, The Links of Stillwater officially opened its doors.</strong>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-inkMuted">
        Turns out, with enough vision, determination, and updated operating systems, anything is possible.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12 text-3xl font-bold">The rebrand</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-inkMuted">
        With the addition of Stillwater, we decided it was time for a rebrand. Apparently having multiple locations
        means you are supposed to look professional or something. So <strong>Lakeville Links</strong> became <strong
          >The Links of Lakeville</strong
        >, alongside <strong>The Links of Stillwater</strong>, under one name: <strong>The Links</strong>. We also
        bought the URL thelinks.golf, because somehow ".golf" is a real thing and honestly, it felt meant to be.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-inkMuted">
        Over the next few months we will keep rolling out the rebrand, updating things, and pretending we fully know
        what we are doing. If you knew the place as Lakeville Links, nothing has changed except the sign. Same bays,
        same bar, same two of us behind it.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-inkMuted">More to come.</p>
      <p class="mt-4 font-semibold">CJ &amp; Cody</p>
    </div>

    {/* 2. The two venues, with the facility facts. */}
    <section class="mt-section">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">The two venues</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        One in the south metro, one in the east. Same bays, same idea, and whichever one is closer to you is the right
        one.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        {
          venues.map((venue) => (
            <li class="rounded border-2 border-ink/15 p-6">
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">
                <a href={venuePath(venue)} class="hover:underline">
                  {venue.data.name}
                </a>
              </h3>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-inkMuted">
                Open since {venue.data.openedYear} · {venue.data.addressLocality}, {venue.data.addressRegion}
              </p>
              {venue.data.intro && <p class="mt-3 text-inkMuted">{venue.data.intro}</p>}
              <div class="mt-6">
                <BookButton venue={venue} size="sm" variant="outline" />
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    {/* 3. Press. Redirect target for the retired /news shell — keep the anchor. */}
    <section class="mt-section" id="press">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">In the press</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        Coverage of both openings, from people who came and looked before writing about it.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-8 divide-y divide-ink/10">
        {
          press.map((item) => (
            <li class="py-4">
              <a href={item.href} class="font-semibold hover:underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                {item.title}
              </a>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-inkMuted">
                {item.outlet} · {item.date}
              </p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <StubNote
        class="mt-6"
        needs="Links only, deliberately. No quotation is reproduced from any of these pieces because none was captured verbatim during handover, and inventing one is not an option. If the client wants pull quotes, send the sentences and the outlet will be credited properly."
      />
    </section>

    {/* 4. Sponsors. Redirect target for /advertisinglogos — keep the anchor. */}
    <section class="mt-section" id="sponsors">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">The bay sponsors</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        Five Lakeville bays carry the name of a local business that backed the place.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
        {
          sponsors.map((sponsor) => (
            <li class="rounded border-2 border-ink/15 p-4">
              <p class="text-sm text-inkMuted">{sponsor.bay}</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-lg font-semibold">{sponsor.name}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      {
        /* Bay 3 is missing from the list above and the numbering makes that
          obvious. A gap mark says so on purpose — it is a real content gap, and
          the alternative is a page that looks as though it cannot count.

          Standalone on the page's white ground rather than as a sixth card: a
          `notSet` cell brings its own greige tint and its own padding, so
          dropping it into a bordered, padded `<li>` double-pads it. Same
          treatment as the winter-membership gap on /memberships. */
      }
      <div class="mt-6 max-w-prose-page">
        <GapCell
          label="Bay 3"
          state="notSet"
          size="name"
          reason="Bay 3 carries no sponsor name. We do not know whether it is unsold or simply not on the list we were given, and we would rather show you the hole in the numbering than quietly renumber the bays and hope nobody counts."
        />
      </div>
      <StubNote
        class="mt-6"
        needs="Sponsor logo files and each sponsor's website, so these become links rather than names. Bay 3 is marked as a gap beside this note — confirm whether it is unsold or simply missing from the handover, and replace the GapCell either way. No Stillwater sponsors exist yet. Also confirm each sponsor's full trading name: these five are read off image filenames, so “Von Hanson” is almost certainly an abbreviation, and a paying sponsor's name printed short is a small error with a large apology attached."
      />
    </section>

    {
      /* 5. Proof. 81% of the segment shows no reviews at all, so this is a real
        differentiator — and as of FW-4000 we have four, every one of them a
        Google review the venue already publishes under a name. Still no invented
        quotes, and still no counts or star ratings: the third-party listings
        disagree with each other on both, so we quote what is attributable and
        count nothing. */
    }
    {
      testimonials.length > 0 && (
        <section class="mt-section">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold">What people say</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
            Left on Google by people who came in. We have not touched a word of them, typos and all.
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
            {testimonials.map((t) => (
              <li class="rounded border-2 border-ink/15 p-6">
                <blockquote class="text-inkMuted">&ldquo;{t.data.quote}&rdquo;</blockquote>
                <p class="mt-4 text-sm font-semibold">
                  {t.data.name}
                  {t.data.source && <span class="font-normal text-inkMuted"> · {t.data.source}</span>}
                </p>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <StubNote
            class="mt-6"
            needs="The permalink for each review, so every quote can link to the review it came from, and the Google Business Profile link for each venue. All four of these are Lakeville: Stillwater has no Business Profile on record and therefore no reviews to quote, which is a reason to create one rather than to borrow a quote from the other venue."
          />
        </section>
      )
    }

    {/* Every page ends in a transactional CTA (playbook-core.md §6). */}
    <section class="mt-section rounded bg-surface p-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Come and see it</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-inkMuted">
        Book an hour at either venue. Bring people who do not golf — nobody has to be any good.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6"><BookButton size="lg" /></div>
    </section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
